    <h2>What a senior check adds</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>A careful look at joints, walk and muscle, and a pain score.</li>
        <li>Blood and urine tests for kidneys, liver, thyroid and diabetes.</li>
        <li>Blood pressure, especially for cats.</li>
        <li>Eyes, ears and teeth, which all change with age.</li>
        <li>Weight, appetite and thirst, tracked visit to visit.</li>
        <li>Memory and behaviour: night-time pacing and confusion can be helped.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Small changes at home that help</h2>
    <p>Non-slip rugs on hard floors, a ramp to the sofa or car, a litter tray with a low side, raised food bowls, and shorter, more frequent walks. We are happy to talk through your home and routine; small things make a big difference to an old body.</p>
    <p class="callout">Drinking more, peeing more, losing weight while eating well: write it down and tell us. Those three are the commonest early signs we look for.</p>
    <h2>Comfort comes first</h2>
    <p>For older pets with long-term conditions we build a plan with you that puts comfort first: the right medicines, regular reviews, and a phone line to a nurse who knows your pet when you are not sure if something is normal.</p>
